To generate a table of contents (TOC) automatically in a LaTeX document, you need to follow these steps:

1. Add the `toc` package to your preamble:

```latex
\documentclass{article}

\usepackage{tocloft} % add this line

\begin{document}
  ...
```

2. Use the `tocloft` package commands to customize the appearance of the TOC:

```latex
\documentclass{article}

\usepackage{tocloft} % add this line

\renewcommand{\cftsecfont}{\bfseries} % change font for section headings
\renewcommand{\cftsecpagefont}{\bfseries} % change font for page numbers
\setlength{\cftsecnumwidth}{2em} % set width for section numbers

\begin{document}
  ...
```

3. Add the `\tableofcontents` command to your document after the `\begin{document}`:

```latex
\documentclass{article}

\usepackage{tocloft}

\renewcommand{\cftsecfont}{\bfseries}
\renewcommand{\cftsecpagefont}{\bfseries}
\setlength{\cftsecnumwidth}{2em}

\begin{document}

\tableofcontents % add this line

\section{First Section}
  ...

\end{document}
```

4. Use sectioning commands (`\section`, `\subsection`, etc.) to create the content for your document.

5. LaTeX will automatically generate the TOC based on the sectioning commands used in your document.

With these steps, you should be able to generate an automatically generated table of contents in your LaTeX document. You can customize the appearance of the TOC using the commands provided by the `tocloft` package.

